{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>You send forth</b> — The men of inquiry say: every living thing, after its death, will rise. And the sages of truth say: the universals are preserved and the particulars perish." "And the meaning of יבראון (they are created) — others. And the discerning will understand from it the way of truth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {0 "Resolved אובדים as 'perish' rather than 'are lost,' maintaining the philosophical universal/particular contrast."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:17.314099633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}